  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Can we get a setting that limits or stops VRChat from rendering the world and avatars when the SteamVR menu button is pressed? I've been having this major issue for a long time and have just been dealing with it. Most of the time when I open SteamVR, my game freezes for a while or completely. This happens only when I open the menu; otherwise, I can play mostly without any issues. Also, these freezes don't cause dropped frames in fpsVR. My wild guess is that this happens because my VRAM is already at its limits. Despite that, I decided to buy a new router (ASUS TUF Gaming BE9400) after years of using a cheap one, but that didn't prevent this from happening. I'm using Steam Link (wireless) on Quest 3, and my GPU is an Asus GeForce RTX 3070 Ti TUF Gaming OC.\n\nMode suggestions: Blurry & Renderless",
